message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and name
  the code revision recorded in the setup of any result you report.
title: cat-model
type: software
authors:
  - name: Artificial Intelligence Underwriting Company
    website: https://aiuc.com
    email: tom@aiuc.com
contact:
  - name: Artificial Intelligence Underwriting Company
    email: tom@aiuc.com
repository-code: https://github.com/aiunderwriting/cat-model
url: https://github.com/aiunderwriting/cat-model
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  Experimental catastrophe model for AI risk. It estimates the distribution of
  annual monetary loss from AI-caused incidents for a declared study year,
  from quantile judgments of a panel of large language models, conditioned on
  forecast AI-capability trajectories, and from a register of assumptions.
keywords:
  - AI risk
  - catastrophe model
  - expert elicitation
  - large language models
